[2026-03-14T20:42:55.485Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AajEz6kEDDyjLdz6qNmZZR","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# LinearClone — Project Management App\n     2→\n     3→A project management application inspired by Linear, designed for software development teams to track issues, plan sprints, and manage projects with a clean, fast, keyboard-friendly interface.\n     4→\n     5→## Core Concepts\n     6→\n     7→- **Workspace**: The top-level container. Each workspace has its own projects, teams, and members. For this app, there is a single workspace.\n     8→- **Team**: A group of members working together (e.g., \"Engineering\", \"Design\"). Each team has its own set of issues, cycles, and views.\n     9→- **Project**: A cross-team initiative that groups related issues toward a larger goal. Projects have a status, target date, lead, and progress bar based on completed issues.\n    10→- **Issue**: The fundamental unit of work. Issues have a title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels, project, and cycle.\n    11→- **Cycle**: A time-boxed iteration (like a sprint). Each team can have one active cycle at a time.\n    12→- **Label**: Tags for categorizing issues (e.g., \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\").\n    13→- **Member**: A user in the workspace who can be assigned issues and belong to teams.\n    14→\n    15→## Authentication\n    16→\n    17→Simple email-based authentication (no OAuth). Users sign up with name, email, and password. On first login, a default workspace is created. Sessions are managed via a session token stored in localStorage.\n    18→\n    19→### Pages\n    20→\n    21→- **Login Page** (`/login`): Email + password fields, \"Sign in\" button, link to sign up.\n    22→- **Sign Up Page** (`/signup`): Name, email, password fields, \"Create account\" button, link to login.\n    23→\n    24→## Navigation\n    25→\n    26→A collapsible left sidebar present on all authenticated pages:\n    27→\n    28→### Sidebar Sections\n    29→\n    30→1. **Workspace Header** — Workspace name at top, clickable to go to home.\n    31→2. **Main Navigation**:\n    32→   - My Issues (icon: user-circle)\n    33→   - Inbox (icon: inbox) — Shows notification count badge\n    34→3. **Team Section** — For each team:\n    35→   - Team name as section header (collapsible)\n    36→   - Issues (icon: list)\n    37→   - Active Cycle (icon: refresh-cw)\n    38→   - Projects (icon: folder)\n    39→   - Views (icon: layout) — Saved filtered views\n    40→4. **Workspace Section**:\n    41→   - All Projects (icon: folder)\n    42→   - All Teams (icon: users)\n    43→   - Members (icon: user-plus)\n    44→   - Labels (icon: tag)\n    45→   - Settings (icon: settings)\n    46→\n    47→The sidebar should be collapsible to icon-only mode via a toggle button.\n    48→\n    49→## Issue Statuses\n    50→\n    51→Issues flow through these statuses (each with a distinct icon and color):\n    52→\n    53→| Status       | Icon         | Color   |\n    54→|-------------|-------------|---------|\n    55→| Backlog      | dotted circle | gray    |\n    56→| Todo         | circle       | gray    |\n    57→| In Progress  | half circle  | yellow  |\n    58→| In Review    | three-quarter circle | blue |\n    59→| Done         | check circle | green   |\n    60→| Cancelled    | x-circle     | red     |\n    61→\n    62→## Issue Priorities\n    63→\n    64→| Priority | Icon            | Color  |\n    65→|----------|----------------|--------|\n    66→| Urgent   | alert-triangle  | red    |\n    67→| High     | arrow-up        | orange |\n    68→| Medium   | minus           | yellow |\n    69→| Low      | arrow-down      | blue   |\n    70→| No Priority | dots-horizontal | gray |\n    71→\n    72→## Pages\n    73→\n    74→### My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n    75→\n    76→A filtered view showing all issues assigned to the current user, grouped by status. Each group is collapsible.\n    77→\n    78→**Issue Row** displays:\n    79→- Priority icon\n    80→- Issue identifier (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n    81→- Title (clickable, navigates to issue detail)\n    82→- Status icon (clickable to change status)\n    83→- Labels as small colored badges\n    84→- Assignee avatar\n    85→- Due date (if set)\n    86→- Project name (if assigned)\n    87→\n    88→**Filters toolbar** at top:\n    89→- Status filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    90→- Priority filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    91→- Label filter (multi-select dropdown)\n    92→\n    93→### Inbox Page (`/inbox`)\n    94→\n    95→Shows notifications for the current user:\n    96→- Issue assigned to you\n    97→- Issue you're subscribed to was updated\n    98→- You were mentioned in a comment\n    99→\n   100→Each notification row shows: icon for type, issue identifier, brief description, relative timestamp.\n   101→Notifications can be marked as read (click) or archived. Unread notifications are visually distinct (bold, left border accent).\n   102→\n   103→### Team Issues Page (`/team/:teamId/issues`)\n   104→\n   105→The primary issue list for a team. Similar layout to My Issues but shows all team issues.\n   106→\n   107→**Features**:\n   108→- Group by: Status (default), Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None\n   109→- Sort by: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status\n   110→- Filter by: Status, Priority, Assignee, Label, Project, Cycle\n   111→- Bulk actions: Select multiple issues via checkboxes, then change status/priority/assignee/label\n   112→- \"New Issue\" button opens a create issue modal\n   113→\n   114→**Issue Row** (same as My Issues but also shows):\n   115→- Checkbox for bulk selection\n   116→- Team identifier prefix (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n   117→\n   118→### Issue Detail Page (`/issue/:issueId`)\n   119→\n   120→Full issue view with inline editing for all fields.\n   121→\n   122→**Left Panel** (main content, ~70% width):\n   123→- Issue identifier and title (inline editable, large font)\n   124→- Status selector (inline dropdown)\n   125→- Description (rich text area, supports markdown, inline editable)\n   126→- **Activity / Comments section** at bottom:\n   127→  - Tab toggle: \"Activity\" | \"Comments\"\n   128→  - Activity tab shows chronological history of all changes (status changes, assignee changes, etc.)\n   129→  - Comments tab shows user comments with avatar, name, timestamp\n   130→  - Comment input box with \"Comment\" button at bottom\n   131→  - Each comment shows author avatar, name, relative timestamp, and content\n   132→\n   133→**Right Panel** (sidebar, ~30% width):\n   134→- **Status**: Dropdown selector showing current status with icon\n   135→- **Priority**: Dropdown selector showing current priority with icon\n   136→- **Assignee**: Searchable member selector with avatar\n   137→- **Labels**: Multi-select label picker with colored dots\n   138→- **Project**: Searchable project selector\n   139→- **Cycle**: Dropdown showing available cycles for the team\n   140→- **Due Date**: Date picker\n   141→- **Created**: Timestamp (read-only)\n   142→- **Updated**: Timestamp (read-only)\n   143→\n   144→**Sub-issues section** (below description):\n   145→- List of child issues\n   146→- \"Add sub-issue\" button\n   147→\n   148→### Create Issue Modal\n   149→\n   150→Triggered from any issues list page via \"New Issue\" button or keyboard shortcut.\n   151→\n   152→**Fields**:\n   153→- Team selector (dropdown, defaults to current team if on a team page)\n   154→- Title (text input, required)\n   155→- Description (text area, supports markdown)\n   156→- Status (dropdown, defaults to \"Backlog\")\n   157→- Priority (dropdown, defaults to \"No Priority\")\n   158→- Assignee (searchable member selector)\n   159→- Labels (multi-select)\n   160→- Project (optional, searchable selector)\n   161→- Cycle (optional, dropdown of team's cycles)\n   162→- Due date (date picker)\n   163→- Parent issue (optional, searchable issue selector for sub-issues)\n   164→\n   165→**Actions**: \"Create Issue\" button, \"Cancel\" button. After creation, show the new issue identifier briefly and navigate to the issues list.\n   166→\n   167→### Active Cycle Page (`/team/:teamId/cycles`)\n   168→\n   169→Shows the team's cycles.\n   170→\n   171→**Cycle List**:\n   172→- Each cycle shows: Name, date range, progress bar (% of issues done), issue count\n   173→- Active cycle is highlighted\n   174→- Click a cycle to view its issues\n   175→\n   176→**Cycle Detail View**:\n   177→- Cycle name and date range at top\n   178→- Progress stats: Total issues, completed, in progress, remaining\n   179→- Progress bar showing completion percentage\n   180→- Issue list (same layout as Team Issues, filtered to this cycle)\n   181→- Burndown-style summary: issues completed per day as a simple bar chart\n   182→\n   183→**Create Cycle**:\n   184→- \"New Cycle\" button\n   185→- Fields: Name, Start date, End date\n   186→- Only one cycle can be active at a time per team\n   187→\n   188→### Projects Page (`/projects`)\n   189→\n   190→Lists all projects across all teams.\n   191→\n   192→**Project Card** displays:\n   193→- Project name (clickable)\n   194→- Status badge (Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled)\n   195→- Lead (avatar + name)\n   196→- Target date\n   197→- Progress bar (issues completed / total)\n   198→- Team icons showing which teams have issues in this project\n   199→\n   200→**Filters**: Status filter, Lead filter, Team filter\n   201→\n   202→**Create Project** button opens a modal:\n   203→- Name (required)\n   204→- Description (text area)\n   205→- Status (dropdown)\n   206→- Lead (searchable member selector)\n   207→- Target date (date picker)\n   208→- Teams (multi-select)\n   209→\n   210→### Project Detail Page (`/project/:projectId`)\n   211→\n   212→**Header**:\n   213→- Project name (inline editable)\n   214→- Status badge (inline editable)\n   215→- Progress bar\n   216→- Target date (inline editable)\n   217→- Lead (inline editable)\n   218→\n   219→**Tabs**:\n   220→- **Issues**: All issues in this project, grouped by team, with standard issue list layout\n   221→- **Overview**: Description (editable), milestones, key metrics\n   222→\n   223→### Members Page (`/settings/members`)\n   224→\n   225→List of all workspace members.\n   226→\n   227→**Member Row**:\n   228→- Avatar\n   229→- Name\n   230→- Email\n   231→- Role (Admin, Member)\n   232→- Teams they belong to (as badges)\n   233→\n   234→**Actions**:\n   235→- \"Invite Member\" button → modal with email field\n   236→- Change role dropdown\n   237→- Remove member (with confirmation)\n   238→\n   239→### Teams Management Page (`/settings/teams`)\n   240→\n   241→**Team Card**:\n   242→- Team name\n   243→- Identifier prefix (e.g., \"ENG\")\n   244→- Member count\n   245→- Active cycle name (if any)\n   246→\n   247→**Create Team** button → modal:\n   248→- Name (required)\n   249→- Identifier prefix (required, uppercase, 2-5 chars)\n   250→- Description\n   251→\n   252→Click a team card to see team settings:\n   253→- Edit name, description, identifier\n   254→- Manage team members (add/remove)\n   255→\n   256→### Labels Page (`/settings/labels`)\n   257→\n   258→**Label List**:\n   259→- Each label shows: Colored dot, name, issue count using this label\n   260→- Edit button (inline edit name and color)\n   261→- Delete button (with confirmation)\n   262→\n   263→**Create Label** button:\n   264→- Name field\n   265→- Color picker (preset colors + custom hex)\n   266→\n   267→### Settings Page (`/settings`)\n   268→\n   269→Workspace-level settings:\n   270→- Workspace name (editable)\n   271→- Default team for new issues\n   272→\n   273→## Keyboard Shortcuts\n   274→\n   275→The app supports keyboard shortcuts for power users:\n   276→- `C` — Open create issue modal\n   277→- `G` then `I` — Go to My Issues\n   278→- `G` then `N` — Go to Inbox\n   279→\n   280→## Visual Design\n   281→\n   282→The app has a clean, minimal, modern design:\n   283→\n   284→- **Color scheme**: Dark mode by default. Background `#0f1117`, surface `#1a1d24`, borders `#2a2d35`, primary accent `#5e6ad2` (Linear's signature purple-blue).\n   285→- **Typography**: System font stack (Inter preferred). Issue titles 14px medium, descriptions 13px regular, labels/metadata 12px.\n   286→- **Spacing**: Compact but readable. Issue rows ~36px height. Generous whitespace in detail views.\n   287→- **Animations**: Subtle transitions on hover states and dropdown opens (150ms ease).\n   288→- **Empty states**: Friendly messages with icons when lists are empty (e.g., \"No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.\")\n   289→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fce00bd2-5cbf-4ef5-a5c6-94d6b48a030d","uuid":"b28f1798-bc14-42e6-9798-dfdb6207ca2c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/apps/LinearClone/AppSpec.md","content":"# LinearClone — Project Management App\n\nA project management application inspired by Linear, designed for software development teams to track issues, plan sprints, and manage projects with a clean, fast, keyboard-friendly interface.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\n- **Workspace**: The top-level container. Each workspace has its own projects, teams, and members. For this app, there is a single workspace.\n- **Team**: A group of members working together (e.g., \"Engineering\", \"Design\"). Each team has its own set of issues, cycles, and views.\n- **Project**: A cross-team initiative that groups related issues toward a larger goal. Projects have a status, target date, lead, and progress bar based on completed issues.\n- **Issue**: The fundamental unit of work. Issues have a title, description, status, priority, assignee, labels, project, and cycle.\n- **Cycle**: A time-boxed iteration (like a sprint). Each team can have one active cycle at a time.\n- **Label**: Tags for categorizing issues (e.g., \"Bug\", \"Feature\", \"Improvement\").\n- **Member**: A user in the workspace who can be assigned issues and belong to teams.\n\n## Authentication\n\nSimple email-based authentication (no OAuth). Users sign up with name, email, and password. On first login, a default workspace is created. Sessions are managed via a session token stored in localStorage.\n\n### Pages\n\n- **Login Page** (`/login`): Email + password fields, \"Sign in\" button, link to sign up.\n- **Sign Up Page** (`/signup`): Name, email, password fields, \"Create account\" button, link to login.\n\n## Navigation\n\nA collapsible left sidebar present on all authenticated pages:\n\n### Sidebar Sections\n\n1. **Workspace Header** — Workspace name at top, clickable to go to home.\n2. **Main Navigation**:\n   - My Issues (icon: user-circle)\n   - Inbox (icon: inbox) — Shows notification count badge\n3. **Team Section** — For each team:\n   - Team name as section header (collapsible)\n   - Issues (icon: list)\n   - Active Cycle (icon: refresh-cw)\n   - Projects (icon: folder)\n   - Views (icon: layout) — Saved filtered views\n4. **Workspace Section**:\n   - All Projects (icon: folder)\n   - All Teams (icon: users)\n   - Members (icon: user-plus)\n   - Labels (icon: tag)\n   - Settings (icon: settings)\n\nThe sidebar should be collapsible to icon-only mode via a toggle button.\n\n## Issue Statuses\n\nIssues flow through these statuses (each with a distinct icon and color):\n\n| Status       | Icon         | Color   |\n|-------------|-------------|---------|\n| Backlog      | dotted circle | gray    |\n| Todo         | circle       | gray    |\n| In Progress  | half circle  | yellow  |\n| In Review    | three-quarter circle | blue |\n| Done         | check circle | green   |\n| Cancelled    | x-circle     | red     |\n\n## Issue Priorities\n\n| Priority | Icon            | Color  |\n|----------|----------------|--------|\n| Urgent   | alert-triangle  | red    |\n| High     | arrow-up        | orange |\n| Medium   | minus           | yellow |\n| Low      | arrow-down      | blue   |\n| No Priority | dots-horizontal | gray |\n\n## Pages\n\n### My Issues Page (`/my-issues`)\n\nA filtered view showing all issues assigned to the current user, grouped by status. Each group is collapsible.\n\n**Issue Row** displays:\n- Priority icon\n- Issue identifier (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n- Title (clickable, navigates to issue detail)\n- Status icon (clickable to change status)\n- Labels as small colored badges\n- Assignee avatar\n- Due date (if set)\n- Project name (if assigned)\n\n**Filters toolbar** at top:\n- Status filter (multi-select dropdown)\n- Priority filter (multi-select dropdown)\n- Label filter (multi-select dropdown)\n\n### Inbox Page (`/inbox`)\n\nShows notifications for the current user:\n- Issue assigned to you\n- Issue you're subscribed to was updated\n- You were mentioned in a comment\n\nEach notification row shows: icon for type, issue identifier, brief description, relative timestamp.\nNotifications can be marked as read (click) or archived. Unread notifications are visually distinct (bold, left border accent).\n\n### Team Issues Page (`/team/:teamId/issues`)\n\nThe primary issue list for a team. Similar layout to My Issues but shows all team issues.\n\n**Features**:\n- Group by: Status (default), Priority, Assignee, Project, Label, None\n- Sort by: Priority, Created date, Updated date, Status\n- Filter by: Status, Priority, Assignee, Label, Project, Cycle\n- Bulk actions: Select multiple issues via checkboxes, then change status/priority/assignee/label\n- \"New Issue\" button opens a create issue modal\n\n**Issue Row** (same as My Issues but also shows):\n- Checkbox for bulk selection\n- Team identifier prefix (e.g., `ENG-42`)\n\n### Issue Detail Page (`/issue/:issueId`)\n\nFull issue view with inline editing for all fields.\n\n**Left Panel** (main content, ~70% width):\n- Issue identifier and title (inline editable, large font)\n- Status selector (inline dropdown)\n- Description (rich text area, supports markdown, inline editable)\n- **Activity / Comments section** at bottom:\n  - Tab toggle: \"Activity\" | \"Comments\"\n  - Activity tab shows chronological history of all changes (status changes, assignee changes, etc.)\n  - Comments tab shows user comments with avatar, name, timestamp\n  - Comment input box with \"Comment\" button at bottom\n  - Each comment shows author avatar, name, relative timestamp, and content\n\n**Right Panel** (sidebar, ~30% width):\n- **Status**: Dropdown selector showing current status with icon\n- **Priority**: Dropdown selector showing current priority with icon\n- **Assignee**: Searchable member selector with avatar\n- **Labels**: Multi-select label picker with colored dots\n- **Project**: Searchable project selector\n- **Cycle**: Dropdown showing available cycles for the team\n- **Due Date**: Date picker\n- **Created**: Timestamp (read-only)\n- **Updated**: Timestamp (read-only)\n\n**Sub-issues section** (below description):\n- List of child issues\n- \"Add sub-issue\" button\n\n### Create Issue Modal\n\nTriggered from any issues list page via \"New Issue\" button or keyboard shortcut.\n\n**Fields**:\n- Team selector (dropdown, defaults to current team if on a team page)\n- Title (text input, required)\n- Description (text area, supports markdown)\n- Status (dropdown, defaults to \"Backlog\")\n- Priority (dropdown, defaults to \"No Priority\")\n- Assignee (searchable member selector)\n- Labels (multi-select)\n- Project (optional, searchable selector)\n- Cycle (optional, dropdown of team's cycles)\n- Due date (date picker)\n- Parent issue (optional, searchable issue selector for sub-issues)\n\n**Actions**: \"Create Issue\" button, \"Cancel\" button. After creation, show the new issue identifier briefly and navigate to the issues list.\n\n### Active Cycle Page (`/team/:teamId/cycles`)\n\nShows the team's cycles.\n\n**Cycle List**:\n- Each cycle shows: Name, date range, progress bar (% of issues done), issue count\n- Active cycle is highlighted\n- Click a cycle to view its issues\n\n**Cycle Detail View**:\n- Cycle name and date range at top\n- Progress stats: Total issues, completed, in progress, remaining\n- Progress bar showing completion percentage\n- Issue list (same layout as Team Issues, filtered to this cycle)\n- Burndown-style summary: issues completed per day as a simple bar chart\n\n**Create Cycle**:\n- \"New Cycle\" button\n- Fields: Name, Start date, End date\n- Only one cycle can be active at a time per team\n\n### Projects Page (`/projects`)\n\nLists all projects across all teams.\n\n**Project Card** displays:\n- Project name (clickable)\n- Status badge (Planned, In Progress, Completed, Cancelled)\n- Lead (avatar + name)\n- Target date\n- Progress bar (issues completed / total)\n- Team icons showing which teams have issues in this project\n\n**Filters**: Status filter, Lead filter, Team filter\n\n**Create Project** button opens a modal:\n- Name (required)\n- Description (text area)\n- Status (dropdown)\n- Lead (searchable member selector)\n- Target date (date picker)\n- Teams (multi-select)\n\n### Project Detail Page (`/project/:projectId`)\n\n**Header**:\n- Project name (inline editable)\n- Status badge (inline editable)\n- Progress bar\n- Target date (inline editable)\n- Lead (inline editable)\n\n**Tabs**:\n- **Issues**: All issues in this project, grouped by team, with standard issue list layout\n- **Overview**: Description (editable), milestones, key metrics\n\n### Members Page (`/settings/members`)\n\nList of all workspace members.\n\n**Member Row**:\n- Avatar\n- Name\n- Email\n- Role (Admin, Member)\n- Teams they belong to (as badges)\n\n**Actions**:\n- \"Invite Member\" button → modal with email field\n- Change role dropdown\n- Remove member (with confirmation)\n\n### Teams Management Page (`/settings/teams`)\n\n**Team Card**:\n- Team name\n- Identifier prefix (e.g., \"ENG\")\n- Member count\n- Active cycle name (if any)\n\n**Create Team** button → modal:\n- Name (required)\n- Identifier prefix (required, uppercase, 2-5 chars)\n- Description\n\nClick a team card to see team settings:\n- Edit name, description, identifier\n- Manage team members (add/remove)\n\n### Labels Page (`/settings/labels`)\n\n**Label List**:\n- Each label shows: Colored dot, name, issue count using this label\n- Edit button (inline edit name and color)\n- Delete button (with confirmation)\n\n**Create Label** button:\n- Name field\n- Color picker (preset colors + custom hex)\n\n### Settings Page (`/settings`)\n\nWorkspace-level settings:\n- Workspace name (editable)\n- Default team for new issues\n\n## Keyboard Shortcuts\n\nThe app supports keyboard shortcuts for power users:\n- `C` — Open create issue modal\n- `G` then `I` — Go to My Issues\n- `G` then `N` — Go to Inbox\n\n## Visual Design\n\nThe app has a clean, minimal, modern design:\n\n- **Color scheme**: Dark mode by default. Background `#0f1117`, surface `#1a1d24`, borders `#2a2d35`, primary accent `#5e6ad2` (Linear's signature purple-blue).\n- **Typography**: System font stack (Inter preferred). Issue titles 14px medium, descriptions 13px regular, labels/metadata 12px.\n- **Spacing**: Compact but readable. Issue rows ~36px height. Generous whitespace in detail views.\n- **Animations**: Subtle transitions on hover states and dropdown opens (150ms ease).\n- **Empty states**: Friendly messages with icons when lists are empty (e.g., \"No issues yet. Create your first issue to get started.\")\n","numLines":289,"startLine":1,"totalLines":289}}}
