[2026-03-14T20:43:16.053Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XRzTdjhGuCuNEgog3gJyPz","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# env-setup\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Documents environment prerequisites that must be in place before running app scripts\n     6→(test, deploy, check). Many command failures stem from missing environment variables or\n     7→locale configuration — verify these before running scripts.\n     8→\n     9→## Required Environment Variables\n    10→\n    11→### Container-level (already set in the worker container)\n    12→\n    13→| Variable | Used by |\n    14→|---|---|\n    15→| `NEON_API_KEY` | test, deploy (Neon branch/project management) |\n    16→| `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` | test (Replay recording uploads) |\n    17→| `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` | deploy (Netlify CLI authentication) |\n    18→| `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` | deploy (Netlify site creation) |\n    19→\n    20→### App-level (in each app's `.env` file)\n    21→\n    22→| Variable | Used by | How to get |\n    23→|---|---|---|\n    24→| `NEON_PROJECT_ID` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`neon_project_id`) or created by deploy script |\n    25→| `DATABASE_URL` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`database_url`) or created by deploy script |\n    26→| `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` | deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`site_id`) or created by deploy script |\n    27→\n    28→### Verifying environment variables\n    29→\n    30→Before running tests or deploy, verify required variables are set:\n    31→\n    32→```bash\n    33→# Container-level\n    34→echo $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5       # should show first chars\n    35→echo $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN | head -c 5  # should show first chars\n    36→\n    37→# App-level (from app directory)\n    38→grep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env\n    39→grep DATABASE_URL .env\n    40→```\n    41→\n    42→If `.env` is missing but the app has been deployed before, populate it from `deployment.txt`.\n    43→See `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Populating `.env` for Redeployments\".\n    44→\n    45→## Locale Configuration\n    46→\n    47→The Netlify CLI requires a valid locale. Containers that lack `en_US.UTF-8` will cause\n    48→`netlify deploy` and `netlify sites:create` to fail with locale errors.\n    49→\n    50→**Workaround**: Prefix Netlify CLI commands with `LC_ALL=C`:\n    51→\n    52→```bash\n    53→LC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod ...\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→See `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Locale Workaround\" for details.\n    57→\n    58→## Node Modules\n    59→\n    60→Before running scripts, verify `node_modules` exists and key dependencies are installed:\n    61→\n    62→```bash\n    63→ls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install\n    64→```\n    65→\n    66→If `@neondatabase/serverless` is missing, run `npm install` from the app directory. Note that\n    67→direct `npx tsx` invocation may fail on this dependency even when installed — always use\n    68→`npm run` wrappers (see `skills/scripts/test.md`).\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fce00bd2-5cbf-4ef5-a5c6-94d6b48a030d","uuid":"d63bc0da-53e9-4522-967b-a1eff6348f25","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/env-setup.md","content":"# env-setup\n\n## Purpose\n\nDocuments environment prerequisites that must be in place before running app scripts\n(test, deploy, check). Many command failures stem from missing environment variables or\nlocale configuration — verify these before running scripts.\n\n## Required Environment Variables\n\n### Container-level (already set in the worker container)\n\n| Variable | Used by |\n|---|---|\n| `NEON_API_KEY` | test, deploy (Neon branch/project management) |\n| `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` | test (Replay recording uploads) |\n| `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` | deploy (Netlify CLI authentication) |\n| `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` | deploy (Netlify site creation) |\n\n### App-level (in each app's `.env` file)\n\n| Variable | Used by | How to get |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NEON_PROJECT_ID` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`neon_project_id`) or created by deploy script |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`database_url`) or created by deploy script |\n| `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` | deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`site_id`) or created by deploy script |\n\n### Verifying environment variables\n\nBefore running tests or deploy, verify required variables are set:\n\n```bash\n# Container-level\necho $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5       # should show first chars\necho $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN | head -c 5  # should show first chars\n\n# App-level (from app directory)\ngrep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env\ngrep DATABASE_URL .env\n```\n\nIf `.env` is missing but the app has been deployed before, populate it from `deployment.txt`.\nSee `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Populating `.env` for Redeployments\".\n\n## Locale Configuration\n\nThe Netlify CLI requires a valid locale. Containers that lack `en_US.UTF-8` will cause\n`netlify deploy` and `netlify sites:create` to fail with locale errors.\n\n**Workaround**: Prefix Netlify CLI commands with `LC_ALL=C`:\n\n```bash\nLC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod ...\n```\n\nSee `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Locale Workaround\" for details.\n\n## Node Modules\n\nBefore running scripts, verify `node_modules` exists and key dependencies are installed:\n\n```bash\nls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install\n```\n\nIf `@neondatabase/serverless` is missing, run `npm install` from the app directory. Note that\ndirect `npx tsx` invocation may fail on this dependency even when installed — always use\n`npm run` wrappers (see `skills/scripts/test.md`).\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
